  "finalText": "All 51 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fix in `apps/extension/src/commands.ts`:\n\n**Problem:** `runCli` had three issues causing stale status-bar state:\n\n1. **`await showInformationMessage(...)` on line 193 blocked the build from starting** — the status bar showed \"indexing...\" while the notification was visible, even though the build hadn't begun.\n2. **`await showErrorMessage(...)` / `await showInformationMessage(...)` after `refreshAll()` blocked the function from returning** — the `finally` block then ran a redundant `refreshAll()`.\n3. **If a notification `await` threw after a successful build**, the `catch` block would overwrite `lastBuildError` and the status bar would show \"build failed\" despite the build succeeding.\n\n**Fix (3 changes in one function):**\n\n| What | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Line 193 notification | `await host.window.showInformationMessage(...)` | `void host.window.showInformationMessage(...)` |\n| Lines 199, 204, 211 notifications | `await host.window.show...(...)` | `void host.window.show...(...)` |\n| `finally` block | `refreshAll()` (redundant) | Removed entirely |\n\nThe `void` prefix fires-and-forgets the notification (VS Code shows it regardless of whether the promise is awaited), so `refreshAll()` runs immediately after `runner.run()` completes and the status bar updates right away — no stale \"indexing…\" or \"no index\" left behind.",
